PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains complete consensus that the required Indium-111 chloride volume is determined by pre-decaying the 8.0 mCi dose from the scheduled 8:00 am administration time back to the December 26, 12:00 pm calibration time, rendering the 4:04 am compounding time algebraically invariant. Accounting for the 76.0-hour interval and standard half-life values (67.2 to 67.3 hours), the required volume to draw is firmly established as 3.65 mL to 3.66 mL. The unadjusted 3.51 mL figure remains recognized as an incorrect clinical distractor resulting from failing to pre-decay the dose.
}

